  <h1>Prepaid Watchdog Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 21 October 2025</p>

  <p>Prepaid Watchdog (“the app”) helps Gauteng prepaid-power customers track token purchases. This policy explains what information the app does and does not collect.</p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Purchase entries:</strong> Rand values, kWh figures, regions, dates, and notes you enter are stored locally on your device only.</li>
    <li><strong>SMS parsing:</strong> When you paste an SMS, it is processed on-device to extract the amount, kWh, and date. The raw message is never uploaded or shared.</li>
    <li>The app does not collect personal identity information, contact details, passwords, or precise location.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>Collected data remains on your device and is used solely to display calculations, histories, and reports. No analytics SDKs, ad networks, or third-party trackers are embedded.</p>

  <h2>3. Admin Access for Support & Development</h2>
  <p>Designated admins may temporarily access your account data only for development, troubleshooting, or support. Access is limited to what is necessary to resolve your request and is audited.</p>

  <h2>4. Contact & Support</h2>
  <p>For assistance, open the app’s <strong>In-app Admin Chat</strong> to message the support team. You can also email us at <a href="mailto:support@prepaidwatchdog.com">support@prepaidwatchdog.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, trade, or share your data with third parties.</p>

  <h2>6. Permissions</h2>
  <p>The app does not request SMS read permission; you may paste messages manually.</p>

  <h2>7. Data Retention & Control</h2>
  <p>Your data remains on the device until you delete entries or uninstall the app. Uninstalling removes all stored data.</p>

  <h2>8. Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>The app targets adult household managers. We do not knowingly collect data from children under 13.</p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>Because data stays on the device, securing your phone or tablet (passcode/biometric lock) protects your information.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>Updates will appear at this URL. Continued use after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

  <p>&copy; 2025 Prepaid Watchdog</p>
